# The Dockerfile has no COPY or ADD — the image is built entirely from apt —
# so nothing from this directory belongs in the build context. Exclude
# everything, then re-admit only the Dockerfile. This keeps .git/, build/
# (where deploy briefly holds the Docker Hub token in .crane-config), and the
# local agent files out of the context, and means a future COPY cannot pick
# up anything that was not explicitly listed here.
*
!Dockerfile
